    "created_at": "2016-11-15T08:58:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-15T08:58:44Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I think your PR is fine.\n\nI'm mostly wondering about the distinction between types and instances, but maybe the distinction only matters if there's syntax for types. E.g., the URL Standard defines URLs (not talking about the IDL interface here). Arguably they're a type, but we don't really make that distinction explicit.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
